{
  "task_id": "shock-analysis-supply",
  "top_k": 5,
  "requirements": [
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_023979fb422e5936d7ac",
      "requirement_type": "PRESERVATION",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 1,
        "line_end": 1,
        "exact_text": "This task is to estimate an investment spending shock to a small open economy (Georgia) using Cobb-Douglas production function to estimate the potential GDP. The investment will last 8 years beginning from 2026, which worths 6.5 billion USD. You are going to collect the relevant data from multiple online sources, populate data in test file, and run the model in excel. You should ONLY use excel for this task (no python, no hardcoded numbers for the cells that needs calculation). Keep all the formulas in the test file you did.\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_420d47ab2aaf4de06daf",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 4,
        "line_end": 4,
        "exact_text": "- Get the PWT database from https://www.rug.nl/ggdc/productivity/pwt/?lang=en and fill the relevant data in column B and C in sheet \"PWT\". HINT: read the PWT metadata sheet to understand the meaning of each variable.\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_02c56ee57f2d760db9b8",
      "requirement_type": "PRESERVATION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 5,
        "line_end": 5,
        "exact_text": "- Use Playwright MCP. Go to IMF WEO database and get the real GDP level, real GDP growth rate from 2000 to 2027. Populate the data into the relevant rows of the sheet \"WEO_Data\". Assume the 2027 real GDP growth rate stay unchanged until 2043 to fill the column. Calculate the relevant real GDP projection based on the extended growth rate.\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_255e2f529082dca880d1",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 6,
        "line_end": 6,
        "exact_text": "- Get Consumption of fixed capital data (annual) from ECB for Georgia https://data.ecb.europa.eu/data/geographical-areas/georgia?reference_area_name%5B0%5D=Georgia and fill Column C in sheet \"CFC data\". Link the capital stock data from \"PWT\", and calculate the depreciation rate using column C&D.\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_a699f9064593a6a2e51f",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 7,
        "line_end": 8,
        "exact_text": "- In the sheet \"Production\", we assume the annual depreciation rate = average depreciation rate of most recent 8 years. Use formula to calculate the number and fill cell B3.\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_bec6fc3f2dfeba13a684",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 10,
        "line_end": 10,
        "exact_text": "- Link the relevant data from other sheets to D6:D27 and E6:E27 in \"Production\", and then use formula to calculate LnK and LnY.\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_6e9c0154ee979ac88f8f",
      "requirement_type": "VALIDATION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 11,
        "line_end": 12,
        "exact_text": "- In HP Filter area, you should figure out using Solver in excel to get a smoothed line of LnZ. HINT: to begin with, link LnZ to Column F, duplicate the LnZ_HP column as place holder, calculate the second-order difference and LnA-Trend as a sanity check (which means the column N should be 0 to begin with). Calculate the objective in P5 and then start solver in excel to the min of objective by changing L6:L27.\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_f1a271b2c4236a30a340",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 14,
        "line_end": 14,
        "exact_text": "- Link K and Y from the relevant sheets - latest K is 2023 and latest Y is 2025. You already got the extended Y from \"WEO_Data\". Calculate K/Y from 2002 to 2023. Extend K by applying a fixed anchor (average K/Y of the most recent 9 yrs).\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_6b458805628d15fcb4b6",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 15,
        "line_end": 15,
        "exact_text": "- Link the HP filtered LnZ trend to fill G36:G57. Use excel formula TREND to extend LnZ trend to 2041. Calculate Ystar_base by using lnZ_trend, Y and capital's share.\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_11c165b03ec133028be1",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 16,
        "line_end": 16,
        "exact_text": "- Link data from sheet \"Investment\" to fill in column I, calculate deltaK and K_With based on what you have.\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_7cef72d98fa65a60dff4",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 17,
        "line_end": 17,
        "exact_text": "- Calculated Ystar_with by the new K_with you got earlier.\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_9f9d78883c32c9ffafe1",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 18,
        "line_end": 19,
        "exact_text": "- Fill in the rest of the table - you have all the data you need.\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_bf1d3f0ca400d13736cc",
      "requirement_type": "OUTPUT_PATH",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/shock-analysis-supply/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 20,
        "line_end": 20,
        "exact_text": "Output answers in `test-supply.xlsx`.\n",
        "source_sha256": "2a2730fffe52db4d9595cdc3d3a7a5108c50c64ee0a6615c571be7d351625af4",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    }
  ],
